# nr-office-comrs-host-runtime: the host process of Microsoft Office automation (`mixdogd office-com-host [--session]`): the apartment thread, the stdin reader, the one-shot and session protocols, the answer and cleanup-line writers, panic containment.

No new crate, no new Cargo.lock package and no new dependency edge between the crate's own dependencies: `host/` uses
mixdog-rt, tokio-util, windows (Win32_System_Com, Win32_System_Threading, Win32_Foundation: all already declared) and
serde_json that mixdog-office-com has. One new edge between workspace crates: mixdog-cli -> mixdog-office-com (below).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/lib.rs

After `pub mod identity;` add:

    pub mod host;

(`pub`: tests/bin/office_com_host_test.rs and mixdog-cli call `host::run_with` / `host::run`; the tests/support scenario
registers `host::Handlers`.)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/Cargo.toml

After the `[[bin]] name = "fake-office-host"` target add the test host binary (host_protocol.rs reads its path as
`CARGO_BIN_EXE_office-com-host-test`):

    [[bin]]
    name = "office-com-host-test"
    path = "tests/bin/office_com_host_test.rs"
    required-features = ["test-support"]

After `[[test]] name = "registry_source"` add:

    [[test]]
    name = "host_protocol"
    path = "tests/host_protocol.rs"

## native/core/crates/mixdog-cli/Cargo.toml

[dependencies], next to `mixdog-exthost-worker = { workspace = true }`:

    mixdog-office-com = { workspace = true }

native/core/Cargo.lock: package `mixdog-cli` gains the dependency "mixdog-office-com" (regenerate offline with `cargo update -w`).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-cli/src/main.rs

In `enum Command`, after the `EffortJudgeHost { .. }` variant (before `ExtWorker`) add the hidden subcommand. The arguments are
passed through whole (`--session` selects the long-lived host), as `SkillRun` passes its own:

    /// The process Microsoft Office automation runs in; started by the core, never by a user.
    #[command(name = "office-com-host", hide = true, trailing_var_arg = true, allow_hyphen_values = true, disable_help_flag = true)]
    OfficeComHost {
        #[arg(allow_hyphen_values = true, value_name = "ARGS")]
        args: Vec<std::ffi::OsString>,
    },

In the `match` on the command, after the `Command::EffortJudgeHost { .. } => ..` arm add:

    Command::OfficeComHost { args } => ExitCode::from(mixdog_office_com::host::run(&args) as u8),

(`host::run` answers 0, or 1 after an error line; it returns only after every COM handle was dropped and the apartment left, so
the exit goes through `main`'s return, never `std::process::exit`.)

## What is not wired by this task

- No protocol row, no compose_flip.rs name (SERVICE_PENDING is untouched): the host is a process, not a service method.
- `host::handlers::registered()` registers the operations that nr-office-comrs-session-lifecycle (the session handler) and
  nr-office-comrs-actions (the one-shot handler) replace `unregistered_session` / `unregistered_one_shot` with; until then every
  action answers "Unsupported Office host action: <action>" as the PowerShell host did for an unknown action.
- route.rs RUST_HOST_FORMATS stays empty (nr-office-comrs-switch-word adds docx).
